    "chaosLab": {
     "title": {
      "id": "Crash server di tengah sinkronisasi & racun koordinat",
      "en": "The mid-sync server crash & poisoned coordinates"
     },
     "scenario": {
      "id": "Pada hari Sabtu pukul 03.15 UTC, server API hulu mengalami kehabisan memori saat menyajikan Halaman 4 dari pengiriman batch berkala. Di tengah pengiriman data, koneksi soket TCP terputus mendadak. Saat cron job berjalan satu jam kemudian, pipeline seorang engineer junior telah memperbarui watermark state sebelum data berhasil ditulis ke disk—akibatnya 150 rekaman gempa hilang permanen, termasuk peringatan tsunami lepas pantai.\n\nPada saat yang sama, stasiun sensor seismik baru di Pasifik Selatan memancarkan data dengan posisi lintang dan bujur terbalik, mengirim `[lat, lon]` alih-alih standar `[lon, lat]`. Pipeline tanpa validasi batas koordinat langsung memasukkan nilai lintang 175 derajat Selatan, merusak layer spasial GIS analitik dan mengacaukan visualisasi peta.",
      "en": "At 03:15 UTC on a Saturday morning, an upstream API server experienced an unexpected memory exhaustion crash while streaming Page 4 of an hourly batch. Halfway through transmission, the TCP connection reset. When the ingestion cron job ran an hour later, a junior engineer's pipeline had updated its state watermark before persisting records to disk—permanently skipping 150 seismic events, including an offshore tsunami warning.\n\nSimultaneously, a newly deployed upstream seismic sensor in the South Pacific began emitting coordinates with longitude and latitude reversed, broadcasting `[lat, lon]` instead of standard `[lon, lat]`. Pipelines without explicit coordinate bounds checking inserted latitudes of 175 degrees South, corrupting spatial GIS layers and breaking downstream dashboard aggregations."
     },
     "breakageReason": {
      "id": "Pipeline tersebut tidak bersifat transaksional dan tidak defensif. Watermark diperbarui sebelum penulisan selesai, sehingga penghentian mendadak menghilangkan data permanen. Pipeline juga tidak memiliki validasi skema masuk, memercayai koordinat geografis dari hulu secara buta tanpa memeriksa bahwa lintang selalu berada dalam rentang -90 sampai 90.",
      "en": "The pipeline was neither transactional nor defensive. It updated its watermark before writes were committed, causing permanent data loss on process termination. It also lacked input schema validation, trusting upstream geographic coordinates blindly without verifying that latitude is strictly bounded between -90 and 90."
     },
     "fixGuide": {
      "id": "1. **Tulis penyimpanan sebelum checkpoint:** Tulis data batch ke DuckDB terlebih dahulu. Hanya ketika penulisan sukses barulah Anda menaikkan watermark dan menyimpan `state.json`.\n2. **Swap berkas atomik:** Tulis ke `state.json.tmp` dan gunakan `os.replace` agar berkas checkpoint tidak pernah tertinggal dalam keadaan rusak sebagian.\n3. **Upsert yang idempoten:** Lakukan deduplikasi berdasarkan `event_id` dan `updated_epoch_ms` agar pemrosesan ulang tidak pernah melipatgandakan baris.\n4. **Karantina ke Dead-Letter Queue:** Validasi lintang antara -90 dan 90 serta bujur antara -180 dan 180. Arahkan koordinat bermasalah ke `dlq/rejected.jsonl` beserta metadata diagnostik.",
      "en": "1. **Commit storage before checkpointing:** Write the analytical batch to DuckDB first. Only when the commit succeeds do you advance the watermark and write `state.json`.\n2. **Atomic state swaps:** Write `state.json.tmp` and use `os.replace` to prevent corrupted half-written checkpoint files.\n3. **Idempotent upserts:** Deduplicate by `event_id` and `updated_epoch_ms` so re-processing a batch after a crash never introduces duplicate rows.\n4. **Dead-Letter Queue quarantine:** Validate latitude between -90 and 90 and longitude between -180 and 180. Route corrupted coordinates to `dlq/rejected.jsonl` with diagnostic metadata."
     },
     "defensivePattern": {
      "id": "Pipeline ingesti harus memperlakukan jaringan dan penyedia data hulu sebagai komponen yang tidak tepercaya dan rentan gagal. Simpan data sebelum memperbarui checkpoint, pastikan penulisan bersifat idempoten, dan karantina data beracun ke DLQ tanpa menghentikan pemrosesan data bersih lainnya.",
      "en": "An ingestion pipeline must treat upstream networks and data producers as untrusted and volatile. Persist data before updating checkpoints, make storage writes idempotent, and quarantine poisoned records into a DLQ without crashing the entire batch."
     }
    },
