       "en": "If a machine crashes or runs out of memory while writing directly to state.json, the file is left half-written and corrupt, destroying the pipeline's checkpoint history. Writing to a temporary file and atomically renaming it guarantees that state.json is either the old valid version or the new valid version, never corrupted."
