       "en": "If a server loses power or the operating system terminates a process mid-write, writing directly to `offsets.json` leaves the file truncated and corrupt, destroying state history. Writing to a `.tmp` file and executing `os.replace` guarantees an atomic rename: the file is always either the complete prior state or the complete new state."
